---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /code/
title: "Code & Architecture | Stefanos Tzortzoglou"
description: "Review the technical stack, Open Source philosophy, and live GitHub telemetry of Stefanos Tzortzoglou."
personSchema: true
mainClass: "flex-grow container mx-auto py-16 px-4"
headPreconnect:
  - "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net"
headStyles:
  - href: "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@2.17.0/devicon.min.css"
    integrity: "sha384-6iv3tXABd3c9DYulXujJl8n22ahn/12f45MomxoPv6jBX4LBE4gNJjfkx5mAKIqR"
pageStyle: |
  /* Contribution grid. The data is fetched at build time (_data/contributions.js) and the
     markup is ours, so this styles real elements rather than overriding a vendor stylesheet. */
  .contrib { --cell: 11px; --gap: 3px; }
  .contrib-grid { display: grid; grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-template-rows: repeat(7, var(--cell)); grid-auto-columns: var(--cell); gap: var(--gap); }
  .contrib-day { width: var(--cell); height: var(--cell); border-radius: 2px; background: #cbd5e1; }
  .contrib-day[data-level="1"] { background: #34d399; }
  .contrib-day[data-level="2"] { background: #059669; }
  .contrib-day[data-level="3"] { background: #047857; }
  .contrib-day[data-level="4"] { background: #064e3b; }
  .dark .contrib-day { background: #334155; }
  .dark .contrib-day[data-level="1"] { background: #065f46; }
  .dark .contrib-day[data-level="2"] { background: #059669; }
  .dark .contrib-day[data-level="3"] { background: #34d399; }
  .dark .contrib-day[data-level="4"] { background: #a7f3d0; }
  /* The weekday axis stays put while a year of columns scrolls under it. */
  .contrib-days { display: grid; grid-template-rows: repeat(7, var(--cell)); gap: var(--gap);
    position: sticky; left: 0; z-index: 1; padding-right: .5rem;
    background: rgb(var(--color-surface)); font-size: .6875rem; line-height: var(--cell); }
  /* One column per week, same width as the day grid, or the labels drift out of step with
     the columns they name. They are wider than a cell and overflow to the right on purpose -
     only every fourth or fifth week carries one. */
  .contrib-months { display: grid; grid-auto-flow: column; grid-auto-columns: var(--cell);
    gap: var(--gap); font-size: .6875rem; margin-bottom: .35rem; }
  .contrib-months span { white-space: nowrap; }
---
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">The Code Behind the <span class="text-brand-accent">Commercial</span></h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-brand-muted leading-relaxed">
            While my day job focuses on driving revenue retention and enterprise implementation, my foundation is
            deeply technical.
            This page bridges my commercial portfolio with my raw GitHub output.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 max-w-6xl mx-auto">

        <div class="bg-brand-surface p-8 rounded-2xl border border-brand-muted/10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
                <i class="fas fa-terminal text-brand-accent" aria-hidden="true"></i> Philosophy & Stack
            </h2>

            <div class="prose dark:prose-invert text-brand-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">
                <p class="mb-4">
                    <strong>I am a pragmatist.</strong> I run a Linux environment because it forces a logical
                    understanding of the system, and I strongly advocate for Open Source tools because transparency
                    beats proprietary black boxes.
                </p>
                <p class="mb-4">
                    I map CRM/ERP systems in raw <strong>SQL</strong> rather than through GUI tools, and work
                    with <strong>Snowflake</strong> on the data side. For campaign execution, I write and hand-tune
                    the HTML behind client email templates.
                </p>
                <p class="mb-4">
                    When troubleshooting <strong>API integrations</strong>, I live in Swagger, OpenAPI, and
                    Insomnia, isolating payload errors long before they require an Engineering escalation.
                </p>
                <p>
                    My GitHub reflects this logical approach. This portfolio is built on a fast, lightweight stack
                    (11ty, Nunjucks, Tailwind CSS) and deployed via GitHub Actions. It features a custom Firebase
                    authentication flow for locked content. The Firebase web config is public by design, as it is in
                    every Firebase web app, so access is enforced where it actually counts: server-side Firestore
                    security rules that let an account read only its own record and reserve approval to the owner.
                    For backend utilities and data formatting, I default to JavaScript and Python.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-4 sm:grid-cols-5 gap-6 text-center">
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-linux-plain text-4xl text-yellow-600 dark:text-yellow-500 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Linux</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-azuresqldatabase-plain text-4xl text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">SQL</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="fas fa-snowflake text-4xl text-blue-500 dark:text-blue-300 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Snowflake</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-terraform-plain text-4xl text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Terraform</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-javascript-plain text-4xl text-yellow-500 dark:text-yellow-300 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">JS</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-python-plain text-4xl text-blue-600 dark:text-yellow-400 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Python</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-html5-plain text-4xl text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-500 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">HTML</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-insomnia-plain text-4xl text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-500 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Insomnia</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-git-plain text-4xl text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-500 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Git</span>
                </div>
                <div class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
                    <i class="devicon-eleventy-plain text-4xl text-slate-800 dark:text-gray-200 group-hover:text-brand-muted transition-colors duration-300" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="text-xs opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">11ty</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-8">

            <div class="bg-brand-surface p-1 rounded-2xl border border-brand-muted/10 shadow-lg overflow-hidden">
                <img src="https://steftzor-github-readme-stats.vercel.app/api?username=steftzor&show_icons=true&hide_border=true&bg_color=0f172a&title_color=10b981&icon_color=3b82f6&text_color=94a3b8"
                    alt="GitHub statistics for steftzor: total stars, commits, pull requests, issues and contributions. Full detail on the GitHub profile linked below." class="hidden dark:block w-full h-auto">
                <img src="https://steftzor-github-readme-stats.vercel.app/api?username=steftzor&show_icons=true&hide_border=true&bg_color=e2e8f0&title_color=059669&icon_color=3b82f6&text_color=334155"
                    alt="" role="presentation" class="block dark:hidden w-full h-auto">
            </div>

            <div class="bg-brand-surface p-1 rounded-2xl border border-brand-muted/10 shadow-lg overflow-hidden">
                <img src="https://steftzor-github-readme-stats.vercel.app/api/top-langs/?username=steftzor&layout=compact&hide_border=true&bg_color=0f172a&title_color=10b981&text_color=94a3b8&icon_color=3b82f6"
                    alt="Most-used programming languages across steftzor's public GitHub repositories, by share of code." class="hidden dark:block w-full h-auto">
                <img src="https://steftzor-github-readme-stats.vercel.app/api/top-langs/?username=steftzor&layout=compact&hide_border=true&bg_color=e2e8f0&title_color=059669&text_color=334155&icon_color=3b82f6"
                    alt="" role="presentation" class="block dark:hidden w-full h-auto">
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>
    <div class="mt-16 max-w-6xl mx-auto w-full">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-brand-text">
            <i class="fab fa-github text-brand-accent" aria-hidden="true"></i> Live Code Activity
        </h3>
        {% if contributions %}
<figure class="contrib bg-brand-surface border border-brand-muted/10 p-6 rounded-xl shadow-lg w-full overflow-x-auto">
    <figcaption class="sr-only">
        {{ contributions.total }} GitHub contributions between {{ contributions.from }} and
        {{ contributions.to }}, shown as a grid of days shaded by how many contributions each holds.
    </figcaption>
    <div class="flex text-brand-muted">
        <div class="contrib-days" aria-hidden="true">
            <span></span><span>Mon</span><span></span><span>Wed</span><span></span><span>Fri</span><span></span>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div class="contrib-months" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- for month in contributions.months %}
                <span>{{ month }}</span>
                {%- endfor %}
            </div>
            <div class="contrib-grid">
                {%- for week in contributions.weeks %}{% for day in week %}
                {%- if day %}<div class="contrib-day" data-level="{{ day.level }}" title="{{ day.label }}"></div>
                {%- else %}<div></div>
                {%- endif %}
                {%- endfor %}{% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        {{ contributions.total }} contributions in the last year.
        <a href="{{ contributions.profile }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-brand-accent underline hover:no-underline">See the profile on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
</figure>
{% else %}
<p class="bg-brand-surface border border-brand-muted/10 p-6 rounded-xl text-brand-muted">
    The contribution data could not be fetched for this build.
    <a href="https://github.com/steftzor" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-brand-accent underline hover:no-underline">See the profile on GitHub</a>.
</p>
{% endif %}
    </div>
